{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-truth-panel-ui-shell-a-01","date":"2026-11-25","lens":"2","surface":"panel","area":"panel/ui-shell","refs":["F-panel-508"],"severity":"S3","title":"When someone joining online pays more than the plan, Approve says it saves all of it but the receipt keeps only the plan price","what":"On Today's Joined online card, a paid row whose online payment is not the plan's amount asks first: 'paid X, but the plan is Y. Approve saves X as paid; the rest stays due.' When X is MORE than the plan price and joining fee, Approve quietly saves only the plan price and joining fee on the receipt. The extra money is in the gym's account with no receipt, and the question promised the opposite. The card also compares against three different totals (the row line, the question and the receipt each use their own).","expected":"An online payment above the plan's total is either refused for Approve or saved in full (with the extra shown as credit), and the question says exactly what will be saved.","evidence":["apps/dashboard/src/crm/ui/JoinedOnlineCard.tsx:42-49","apps/dashboard/src/crm/ui/JoinedOnlineCard.tsx:69-72","apps/dashboard/src/crm/ui/JoinedOnlineCard.tsx:174-179","apps/dashboard/src/crm/logic/joinPay.ts:58-63","apps/dashboard/src/crm/logic/joinPay.ts:128-142"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"join-overpay-capped-no-receipt","who":"owners and desk approving online joins","how_often":"rare, only when the paid amount differs from the plan's price","fix_line":"Use one total everywhere and never cap a real payment silently: refuse or keep the extra as credit","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
